# kk: Lower fpow to exp2(log2(a) * b)
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46402 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Lower fpow to exp2(log2(a) * b)

Shaders that preserve inf and NaN get pow as Metal's precise::pow, which is several times slower than precise::exp2 and precise::log2. Vulkan defines the precision of pow as inherited from exp2(y * log2(x)), so set lower_fpow and let NIR emit that form.

Special values follow the lowered expression: pow(0, 0), pow(inf, 0), pow(NaN, 0), pow(1, inf) and pow(x, y) with x < 0 return NaN. These are outside pow's defined domain or covered by the inherited precision.

In Enshrouded (through Wine), average frame rate goes from 30.3 to 32.2 FPS (+6.3% over three paired runs) and the 1% low improves by about 20%.

Testing (Apple M5 Pro, macOS 27.2): dEQP-VK glsl.builtin.precision.pow (fp32 and fp16) passes, and there are no regressions on a 4,496 case shader math list and a 79,312 case list against main.
